            <div xml:id="d683">

                <pb facs="0913" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1731/197: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-10T02:00:00-06:00">March 10, 1936—2
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:25 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>74. As we are now in accord on all points, Nicaraguan negotiators (Francisco
                    Castro and Federico Sacasa) have just informed me that agreement can be signed
                    Wednesday afternoon March 11th. Minister for Foreign Affairs was not present at
                    tonight’s session, hence I am unable now to specify hour of signature. He will
                    sign for Nicaragua as Leonardo Argüello. My exact signature is Arthur Bliss
                    Lane.</p>
                <p>Shall telegraph as soon as possible proposed hour of signature.</p>
                <p>I hope that the Department notwithstanding the foregoing will answer
                    affirmatively my 66, March 9, noon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
